# Hustle {U/R} (CR 107.4e, 508.1d): "Target creature attacks or blocks this turn if able." Cast at Bot2's turn 4 upkeep on Bot2's
# Ornithopter (cast turn 2, so it can attack), paid with blue for the hybrid symbol (Mox Sapphire). Mox Jet is not a creature, so
# it is not a legal target. Ornithopter must attack: declaring no attackers is refused on turn 4 and it attacks
# Bot1 (a 0/2: Bot1 stays at 20). The requirement is for that turn only: on turn 6 Bot2 declares no
# attackers. Mox Jet, Bot1's other mana, stays untapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Hustle // Bustle
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Hustle // Bustle.Cast(Ability: Hustle; Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet)
Bot1.Hand.Hustle // Bustle.Cast(Ability: Hustle; Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
! Bot2.Attack()
Bot2.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot1)
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack()

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Tapped = false
Stack.Count = 0
